quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,203,"Remember Allah in the appointed days. If anyone is in a hurry to depart after two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever stays on, nor is there any sin upon him (either). This (dispensation) is for him who is God-conscious. Be God-conscious, and know that you shall be gathered to Him."
  2,204,"Among the people, there may be someone whose views about worldly life seem impressive to you, and he holds Allah witness to what is in his heart, yet he is the most violent of opponents."
  2,205,"And if he turns away, he tries to cause corruption and disorder in the land, and he ruins crops and livestock. And Allah does not like corruption."
  2,206,"When it is said to him: ‘Be God-conscious’, his arrogance leads him to (more) sins. So, Hell is sufficient for him. It is indeed an evil abode."
  2,207,"Moreover, among the people, there may be someone who sells his life seeking Allah’s pleasure, and Allah is Most Kind to (His) servants."
  2,208,"O believers! Submit all of you to Allah, and do not follow in Satan’s footsteps. He is indeed your manifest enemy."
  2,209,"If you stumble after clear proofs have come to you, then know that Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  2,210,"Are they waiting for Allah (Himself) to come to them in the shades of the clouds, together with the angels, for the matter to be settled (at once)? And to Allah, all matters will be returned."
